# {{.ProductName}}

A Wails v3 desktop app generated from [wails-kit](https://github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit)'s
project template. `main.go` wires [`kit`](https://github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit/tree/main/kit)
and [`kit/wailsbridge`](https://github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit/tree/main/kit/wailsbridge)
into a real Wails app; `frontend/` is a vanilla TypeScript + Vite frontend
(no framework lock-in) with a settings page rendered from the backend's
schema, theme wiring, a health status badge, and an update toast already
built.

## Before your first build

wails-kit v2 is not yet published as a tagged Go module or npm packages (see
its `docs/v2-roadmap.md`, OQ-1/OQ-2). Until then:

1. **Go module.** Point `github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit/v2` at a local
   checkout:

   ```sh
   go mod edit -replace github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit/v2=../path/to/wails-kit
   go mod tidy
   ```

   (This is also why, if you generated this project yourself with
   `wails3 init`, you needed `-skipgomodtidy` — the automatic `go mod tidy`
   step `wails3 init` runs would otherwise fail trying to fetch an
   unpublished module.)

2. **npm packages.** `frontend/package.json` depends on `@wails-kit/types`,
   `@wails-kit/settings`, and `@wails-kit/i18n` at `^2.0.0`, which aren't on
   the npm registry yet either. Point them at the same checkout's `frontend/`
   directory before `npm install`:

   ```sh
   cd frontend
   npm pkg set dependencies.@wails-kit/types=file:../../path/to/wails-kit/frontend/types
   npm pkg set dependencies.@wails-kit/settings=file:../../path/to/wails-kit/frontend/settings
   npm pkg set dependencies.@wails-kit/i18n=file:../../path/to/wails-kit/frontend/i18n
   npm install
   ```

Once wails-kit v2.0.0 is tagged and its npm packages are published, delete
the `go.mod` replace directive and reset these three dependencies to a real
version range (see `go.mod`'s comment for the Go-side follow-up).

## Development

```sh
task dev      # wails3 dev — hot-reloading frontend, live-rebuilt Go
task build    # production build (frontend + Go binary)
task package  # OS-native package (.app / .exe / binary)
task run      # run the last build
```

## What's already wired

- **Settings** — `frontend/src/main.ts` renders a form from
  `settings.Binding.GetSchema()` / `GetValues()` and saves via `SetValues()`.
  Add your own fields with `kit.WithSettingsGroup(...)` in `main.go` — see
  [`settings/README.md`](https://github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit/tree/main/settings).
- **Appearance** — the window background, and the frontend's `data-theme`
  attribute, both follow `appearance:changed`. See
  [`appearance/README.md`](https://github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit/tree/main/appearance).
- **Health** — a badge in the header calls `health.Binding.GetSnapshot()` and
  refreshes on `health:changed`. Register your own checks with
  `kit.WithHealthCheck(...)` — see
  [`health/README.md`](https://github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit/tree/main/health).
- **Updates** — a toast listens for `updates:available` / `:downloading` /
  `:ready` / `:error`. Disabled until you call `kit.WithGitHubRepo(...)` in
  `main.go` (commented out by default) — see
  [`updates/README.md`](https://github.com/jrschumacher/wails-kit/tree/main/updates)
  for the required release-asset naming and signing setup before shipping
  updates to real users.
- **Releases** — `task release` builds, signs (macOS), archives, and uploads
  to a Homebrew tap, reading everything from `.wails-kit.yml`. Fill that file
  in before using it.

## Project layout

```
main.go              — composition root: kit.New, application.New, wailsbridge.Attach/ManageWindow
.wails-kit.yml        — app identity + release config (taskfiles/release.yml reads this)
Taskfile.yml           — dev/build/package/run tasks + wails-kit's shared release Taskfile
taskfiles/release.yml — copied from wails-kit; do not hand-edit, re-copy on update
frontend/
  src/main.ts          — settings form, theme wiring, health badge, update toast
  index.html
build/                 — generated by `wails3 init` / `wails3 generate build-assets`
```
